e2ffe34 feat(macos): auto now prefers native-arm64 per owner promotion ruling
 tools/iolab-launcher/macos_cli.go                 |  2 +-
 tools/iolab-launcher/macos_profile_select.go      | 55 +++++--------
 tools/iolab-launcher/macos_profile_select_test.go | 96 +++++++++++++++++------
 3 files changed, 94 insertions(+), 59 deletions(-)
commit e2ffe34f8d690b3e79654210d98032b1130c7981
Author: Rohan Punj <76807798+rohan-punj@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Thu Aug 20 18:13:16 2026 -0400

    feat(macos): auto now prefers native-arm64 per owner promotion ruling
    
    A bare "auto" profile selection (no --profile flag, no persisted owner
    choice) previously short-circuited to rosetta-amd64 unless a test-only
    IOLBOX_TEST_PREFER_NATIVE=1 hook was set. Following the owner's formal
    promotion ruling (docs/macos-m7-phase6-handoff.md, "Owner promotion
    ruling" / "Owner personally validated..."), and plan section 13's
    PROMOTE clause, auto now runs the same non-mutating nativePreflight used
    for forced and persisted native selections and prefers native-arm64
    whenever it passes (Source "auto-native").
    
    The explicit Rosetta fallback the PROMOTE clause requires is retained
    unchanged: any failing preflight check, or a profiles.env with no
    native-arm64 row, still degrades to rosetta-amd64 with Source
    "auto-fallback-rosetta" and a FallbackReason -- auto never errors out.
    Forced native-arm64 still fails closed.
    
    Removes the now-dead test-only policy hook entirely: the
    IOLBOX_TEST_PREFER_NATIVE env var, the testPreferNativeEnv constant,
    testPreferNativeFromEnv, and the testPreferNative parameter plumbed
    through resolveProfileSelection and its one macos_cli.go caller. Tests
    gain a portable stub limactl so the preflight-passes path is actually
    exercised rather than always falling back.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

